# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc

# OpenCode session memory — agent-local state, never committed.
.opencode/memory/
.opencode/progress.md

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

build/

# Dev sandbox markers — the opt-in "start something in the container" signal.
# Local to each machine; never committed.
.dev/

# fyne-cross working directory (Docker cross-build outputs).
fyne-cross/

# fyne package injects a metadata file into the package directory while it
# builds, then removes it. Without these rules `go build` sees an untracked
# file and stamps vcs.modified=true into a cross-built crower-gui.
cmd/crowergui/fyne_metadata_init.go
cmd/crowergui/fyne_pprof.go
cmd/crowergui/*.syso
cmd/crowergui/crowergui
cmd/crowergui/crowergui.exe
cmd/crowergui/crower-gui
cmd/crowergui/crower-gui.exe
